 "note": "Jimjam's adapter onto the material library (core/materials/PLAN.md). Families are JMAT keys (src/60-jj-mat.js). Jimjam paints in full colour with a white instance tint, so every set keeps its own colour and brightness (tint.keep 1, mean null). scale is world metres per tile [width, height]: the bricks are sized so a stretcher reads about 0.24 m long (the library bricks are chunkier than the procedural 0.24 x 0.08 m ones, so courses read about 0.12 m); the marble keeps the procedural 2.4 m tile (1.2 x 0.6 m blocks), the plaster 4 m. The domes, the sunray and the shaft panels map over their mesh UVs, so their scale is nominal (the dome repeats are in 60-jj-mat.js). Run python3 tools/textures/pack.py settlements/jimjam after any change, then python3 build.py; ?mat=proc shows the procedural look. The shared Ancients MAT (white, rust, verdigris, concrete) takes library sets too (KMAT.bindMat at the end of 60-jj-mat.js); MAT.brick shares the brick row. rust stays procedural: the Ancients meshes stretch their UVs along beams and tanks, and every library rust (plate, scan) smeared into stripes there, where the procedural noise was made for it.",
